# CONTENT

<u><b>MATH RESOURCES AND TEXTBOOKS</b></u>

<b>ladw</b> - Linear Algebra Done Wrong - <i>Sergei Treil</i> -
<a href="https://sites.google.com/a/brown.edu/sergei-treil-homepage/linear-algebra-done-wrong">link</a><br>
A nice middle-ground for learning LA through intuitive proofs,
but an approach through matrices/determinants (like engg. students have to :/).

<b>ladr</b> - Linear Algebra Done Right - <i>Sheldon Axler</i> -
<a href="https://linear.axler.net/">link</a><br>
An abstract approach to LA using linear operators on FDVS to simplify proofs.
More engaging mathematically, but may not cover many applications.

<b>diffyqs</b> - Notes on Differential Equations - <i>Jiří Lebl</i> -
<a href="https://www.jirka.org/diffyqs/">link</a><br>
Explains DEs nicely with sufficient rigour (useful for engg. students).

